  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nHi,\n\nI'm having trouble switching between light and dark themes from my profile icon.\nIt doesn't do anything; it doesn't respond. It's turned black, and I want it to be white. I can't change it.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nGo to the icon in the upper-right corner where the user profile is located. There, you can change the theme, select a language, and log in. Or, if you're already logged in, your preferences will appear. In either case, changing the theme doesn't work. The result is the same with other browsers, such as Edge and Firefox.\n\n### Impact\n\nThe software works, but visually I can't set it to the light theme.\n\n### Additional information\n\nMy environment:\n- Ubuntu Server 26\n- Portainer\n- Homarr stack\n- Connected to Active Directory via LDAP\n- Version 1.77.1 (also happens with some earlier versions)\n\n### Version\n\n1.77.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nEdge (Chromium)",
